# M9 — Single-Node Undeniable Product Proof

Close the complete terminal operator journey on one node, through supported product and public contract surfaces, for one explicitly selected deployment profile.

## Why this is next

[`sequence.v1.json`](../program/sequence.v1.json) makes M9 depend on M8, and so transitively on M0–M8: constitutional core, deployment/fencing truth, the generic pursuit and result seam, the flagship OutcomeRoom, participants and local agents, honest product workspaces, local action semantics, and the enterprise learning/provider-exit boundary. Those stages establish each boundary in isolation. M9 introduces no new object; it joins the boundaries into one journey an outside operator can traverse, and it requires terminal Rust ownership for every route that journey touches. Prerequisites are verified M1–M8 for the selected profile plus all applicable `required_now` and selected `conditional` `PG-*` gates; the sovereign-local lane additionally requires a locally permitted exact-effect authority path, and the managed overlay additionally requires the managed wallet v3 path and its selected conditional gates.

