## In scope

- `M9.1` integrate the compact and advanced package/genesis paths to identical objects and hashes.
- `M9.2` implement and prove two distinct authority lanes. The minimum sovereign-local lane uses deployment-local authentication, a low-risk local product session, a locally permitted nonportable exact-effect authority provider, daemon-side request/subject/equality/constraint verification, revocation, the exact `TemporalVerificationProfile` and `TemporalValidityEvaluation`, and recovery. The ordered managed-optionality overlay adds provider-neutral account/session, WebAuthn begin/finish, factor/guardian lifecycle, the exact request → canonical review → presentation evidence → authenticator ceremony chain, typed exact/batch/standing authorization subjects, `AuthorityReviewReceipt`, a context-bound v3 grant, portable-principal resolution, and the same daemon-side and temporal checks. Passing the local lane never implies the managed lane.
- `M9.3` run the contract-pulled Authority Gateway attach proof against one existing coding agent and one declared MCP server. It is an acceptance slice inside Horizon 1A — not a new application, surface track, runtime, plane, canonical object, or peer work package — and activates only after the selected M3–M5 contract paths and the applicable local-agent, MCP, tool-contract, authority, receipt, and final-invoker paths close their stage gates. Product controls enter the Work, Developer Workspace, Developer Console, Governance, and Provenance contexts only as their owner contracts become operable.
- The selected gateway journey: declared coding-agent installation plus declared MCP server → supported adapter/gateway attach in audit mode → discover exact application, runtime, server, tool, route, and version facts → attribute actor, principal, Session, GoalRun, OutcomeRoom, and request where evidence supports it, retaining confidence, conflicts, and unknowns → observe one proposed sensitive effect without granting or blocking it → show the operator the exact effect, policy result, and evidence → obtain the selected exact-action authorization and the authority artifact the profile requires (`CapabilityLease` when `wallet.network` portable delegation is applicable) → daemon recomputes and revalidates the effect at the final invoker → allow exactly once in the positive branch → block before the invoker in the refusal, substitution, expiry, and revocation branches → admit effect-bound success/refusal receipts and the resulting `WorkResult`/`OutcomeDelta`/room lineage → export content-bound `EnforcementCoverageDeclaration` snapshots and the evidence index.
- For every selected action class the retained `EnforcementCoverageDeclaration` assesses `discovered | observable | attributable | mediated | preventable | receipted` independently, and each asserted property binds concrete mechanism and version, privilege level, deployment scope, bypass assumptions and tested resistance, online and offline behavior, fail-open/fail-closed posture, decision source, final invoker, and evidence refs. Discovery does not imply observation; observation does not imply attribution; attribution does not imply mediation; mediation does not imply prevention; a receipt does not prove an unobserved external effect. `uncovered: true` is the mutually exclusive terminal state for an exact scope; partial gaps keep unsupported facts `false` or `unknown` and record `known_gaps`; opaque actions outside an admitted adapter, gateway, broker, or instrumented effect boundary remain explicitly uncovered.
- Audit attachment grants no authority and makes no prevention claim; moving one selected action class from audit to active enforcement requires an explicit admitted configuration transition and receipt. The coding-agent adapter and MCP binding remain protocol clients — they may observe, attribute, propose, and transport, but cannot mint identity, policy, authority, accepted state, or receipts — and both selected ingress paths converge on the same policy-enforcement point, applicable `AuthorityGrant`/`CapabilityLease` crossing, final invoker, and receipt spine. Any route census, comparison manifest, or retained exit log stays explicitly private and non-canonical.
- `M9.4` run the terminal room, GoalRun, local-agent, verification, and exact repository-effect path end to end while proving complete externally reachable route classification and identical native/MCP policy-enforcement and final-invoker coverage.
- `M9.5` prove daemon restart, Session replacement, provider removal, stale head, revoked grant, substituted effect, deposed writer, uncertainty spanning expiry, whole-VM rollback, lost re-anchor, timeout, and retry behavior.
- `M9.6` export one immutable evidence index and verify integrity, valid-as-of posture, and currentness as separate conclusions offline.
- `M9.7` run first-time operator studies and measure vocabulary exposure, blocker recovery, time to preview/genesis/value, completion, evidence comprehension, and repeat use.
- `M9.8` run signed install and update admission, rollback/recall, manifest-complete backup, secret-safe prepare/apply/cancel restore, temporal-floor handoff/revalidation, forward-only activation, persistent cleanup reconciliation, archive, uninstall-without-wipe, and retirement through the product.
- `M9.9` publish only the claim level supported by the retained evidence.
- Own `platform-operability-observability-and-incidents`, the selected backend-capability declaration, and the selected workload-isolation binding for the sovereign profile, and aggregate the selected M3 information-flow, receipt, and Agentgres mechanisms. HypervisorOS node-root and cTEE/task-capsule claims remain separately future-gated. This does not establish multi-node continuity.
- Own the Governance, Provenance, Developer Console, and Environments operational-journey records for the selected sovereign/managed profile, joining their literal exits without inferring federation or multi-node continuity.
- Pulled product: the first standalone Hypervisor minimum-L0 profile plus the supporting workspaces and owner applications.

## Out of scope

- Multi-node or two-failure-domain continuity, and any inference of it from a joined single-node aggregate (M10).
- Same-system distributed work and embodied pre-live proof (M11); AIIP federation contract (M12); two-sovereign operation (M13); connected/secured services, marketplaces, and demand-gated L1 (M14).
- Any new canonical object, plane, runtime, or application invented to serve the gateway acceptance slice; adjacent substrate never waives the full M1–M8 verification prerequisite.
- `ioi.ai` Goal Space participation outside the separately claimed managed-optionality overlay.

