## Exit proof

The stage exit is owned by the aggregate record `m9-selected-profile-aggregate-exit-and-claim-publication` named in [`sequence.v1.json`](../program/sequence.v1.json), which joins the complete 22-step journey, the sovereign lane, the optional managed overlay, Authority Gateway coverage, lifecycle and offline evidence, the release supply chain, the applicable PG gates, the frozen metrics, the stop rules, and the permitted claim. For that aggregate to become `verified`, all of the following must be true:

- one independent operator completes every terminal step without hidden edits or unavailable one-off tools;
- zero unauthorized final-invoker calls and zero duplicate effects occur in the adversarial matrix;
- all selected state reconstructs after restart and export;
- model-route replacement meets the frozen quality, latency, cost, and custody threshold;
- the declared coding agent and MCP server complete the audit-to-enforcement journey, the allowed branch executes once, every selected refusal branch reaches zero final-invoker calls, and the exported coverage declaration names both proven and intentionally uncovered seams without upgrading either;
- the evidence index links every package, identity, authority, pursuit, verification, effect, outcome, learning, recovery, and lifecycle root;
- each selected P1 child retains its record-declared literal exit, the dependency/child digest matches the joined records, and the aggregate retains exactly one `M9_SELECTED_PROFILE_AGGREGATE_EXIT_AND_CLAIM_PUBLICATION_EXIT=0`; Workstation, Infrastructure, P2, P3, and HypervisorOS/FUTURE records do not close through this aggregate.

The gateway slice additionally fails if an unclassified route starts, audit mode changes an effect, the adapter or MCP server can self-authorize, an expired/revoked/substituted request reaches the invoker, a disconnected observer is reported as preventative, a success receipt is issued without the external effect evidence the selected profile requires, or any coverage claim exceeds the retained mechanism evidence.

## Blocks advancement

- Unverified M1–M8 for the selected profile, or any selected route lacking terminal Rust ownership.
- Any unmet child dependency, including the M3 records the aggregate depends on: `agentgres-production-readiness-and-branch-effects`, `production-information-flow-and-declassification`, `production-receipt-checkpoint-and-offline-proof`.
- Unclosed `PG-*` gates in [`mechanism-gates`](../modules/mechanism-gates.md): `PG-1.3` and `PG-7.5` (terminal product and release supply chain), `PG-2.1` (managed overlay), `PG-3.2` (gateway equivalence and coverage), `PG-6C.1`/`PG-6C.2`/`PG-6C.3` (measured substrate), `PG-7.1`/`PG-7.2`/`PG-7.7`/`PG-7.8` (operability and incidents), plus every other gate the owning records select.
- The external gate `applicable-pg-profile-gates`: a gate closes only in the owning work-item record's retained evidence.
- Any unresolved canon gap below that the proof depends on.
- Ordering: the managed-optionality overlay follows sovereign-local completion and may never substitute for the local lane.

## Nonclaims

- No production SLA beyond closed gates; no multi-node continuity, federation, physical action, public settlement, or universal correctness.
- Passing the sovereign-local lane never implies the managed lane; portable authority is claimed only for the admitted overlay; no blanket passkey-understanding or required-managed-service claim.
- Audit attachment grants no authority and asserts no prevention. Passing the gateway slice proves only the named agent, server, versions, action classes, deployment posture, and tested paths — not universal interception, endpoint-wide control, or coverage of opaque third-party runtimes.
- No hardware assurance claim derived from simulated measurement.
- Lifecycle success cannot promote authority, currentness, product readiness, or stage status by prose; a workflow review hash chain is not product authority.
- Private route censuses, comparison manifests, and exit logs remain non-canonical workflow evidence.

